  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The current best is config_031 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.678). The largest single improvement came from switching concat→weighted fusion (+4.6%), and SCVI gave a modest boost over PCA. The one major untested axis in the current best is the image encoder: we have only used resnet50, which alone scored a very weak 0.208. Config_037 changes only the image encoder to imagenet_vit_l (a substantially larger, pretrained ViT), keeping the otherwise-best settings (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted). This directly tests whether a stronger image encoder can extract more informative morphological features that complement the RNA signal under weighted fusion. If it improves, it justifies further investment in the image branch; if it does not, it confirms the image modality's marginal contribution is encoder-limited and we should focus remaining budget on RNA-side or fusion refinements. This is a clean single-variable extension of the current best, making it the highest-information next experiment under a tight budget."
}

